  {
   "id": "EMWitnIeFQAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
   "author": "cec41188340e8212",
   "date": "2017-01-04T04:33:30Z",
   "subject": "Re: branch line thickness",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This is complicated, since tips don&#39;t have bootstrap value, and we need to assign parent status to tips.<br><br><div><br>require(ggtree) <br>## you need github version of ggtree and treeio<br></div><div>## treeio::read.newick can parse node label as separated support value.<br></div><div>x = read.newick(&#39;RAxML_Zingiberaceae.tre&#39;, node.label=&#39;support&#39;)<br>edge = x@phylo$edge<br>edge = as.data.frame(edge)<br>edge = edge[edge[,2] &lt;= Ntip(x), ]<br><br>df = x@data<br>merge(df, edge, by.x=&quot;node&quot;, by.y=&quot;V1&quot;, all.x=F, all.y=T) -&gt; df2<br>df3= df2[, c(3, 2)]<br>colnames(df3) = colnames(df)<br>x@data = rbind(df3, df)<br><br>ggtree(x, aes(size=I(support/100)))<br><br><br><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 4, 2017 at 5:09 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cool_a...@web.de</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ksS3jkV3KHw/WGwTHULmb4I/AAAAAAAAAA4/9vBxFTwcJLwnS33vns_gJhqgGoKq-NspACLcB/s1600/Clipboard01.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ksS3jkV3KHw/WGwTHULmb4I/AAAAAAAAAA4/9vBxFTwcJLwnS33vns_gJhqgGoKq-NspACLcB/s1600/Clipboard01.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482829176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gVMCdtNQKP1SeJvIO6WQO\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ksS3jkV3KHw/WGwTHULmb4I/AAAAAAAAAA4/9vBxFTwcJLwnS33vns_gJhqgGoKq-NspACLcB/s320/Clipboard01.png\" height=\"211\" width=\"320\" border=\"0\"></a></p>Unfortunately the branch thickness stays at 1 until it either hits a tip node or another node with &gt;70, even if the next split has only a bootstrap value of &lt;70.<span><br><br><br><br>Am Dienstag, 3. Januar 2017 04:31:12 UTC+1 schrieb Yu, Guangchuang:</span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">something like this:<br><br>ggtree(tr, aes(size=label &gt; 80)) + scale_size_manual(values=c(1, .1))<br><br></div></span><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><span>On Mon, Jan 2, 2017 at 1:14 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">cool_a...@web.de</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">Is it possible to make branches thicker if the node is supported by a bootstrap value greather than x?<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div></span><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because 